🔥StartUpOptimization:
Startup optimization is the process to reducing time to take app open and become interactive

🔥StartUp Type:

🔸Cold Start[slowest]
Usually the slowest because the process and app components need initialization.
🔹Flow:
App Open -> Linux Create Process -> Application OnCreate() -> Activity OnCreate() -> Activity Start() -> Activity Resume
🔹Example:
Force-stop the app and launch it again.


🔸Warm Start[on Back press]
Usually faster than a cold start because the process already exists.
🔹Flow:
App Open -> process Already Create -> Activity OnCreate()-> Activity Start() -> Activity Resume
🔹Example:
The user launches the app again.


🔸Hot Start[press Home Button]
Usually the fastest because the Activity does not need to be recreated.
🔹Flow:
App Open ->  Activity already Exist-> Activity ReStart() -> Activity Start()-> Activity Resume
🔹Example:You press Home


🔥How to Optimize StartUp

🔸Lazy Initialization
Used for Analytical event because it is used when needed

🔸Coroutine for differed and background work
Use for Reading local file ,loading non critical config

🔸Work manager for differed and persistence work
Syncing data with network constraints and retries

🔥BaseProfile:
BaseLine profile is list of important app  method that android compile during installation so app start faster and perform better

🔹With Base Profile :
Dev create base profile -> include inside APk ->  installApp -> ART observer and compile method ->App start faster

🔹Without Base Profile :
InstallApp -> ART observes frequently used methods ->JIT compiles them while app is running -> Performance gradually improves

🔹 code syntax:

@RunWith(AndroidJUnit4::class)
class BaseProfileGenerator{
@get:rule
 val rule = BaseProfileRule()

@Test
fun generate(package: com.example.text,includeInStartUpProfile = true)
{
rule.collect{
 pressHome()
 startActivityAndWait()
 device.waitForIdeal()
 login()
}
}
